---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Project" description="Learn about the HORUS OS project: its direction, engineering philosophy, and Arch-based foundation.">
<div class="ambient-background"></div><div class="precision-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></div><Header />
<main class="editorial-page"><div class="container container--md"><header class="page-header"><p class="page-kicker">Project / Direction</p><h1 class="page-title">A distribution is a set of decisions.</h1><p class="page-lead">HORUS OS is an independent Arch-based Linux distribution in development, focused on a considered desktop experience, practical performance, and maintainable engineering.</p></header>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Why HORUS OS?</h2><div><p>Linux offers an extraordinary range of distributions, but most fall into established categories: minimal and unopinionated, or batteries-included with varying degrees of visual polish. HORUS OS explores a different position: deliberate engineering decisions combined with cohesive visual identity, without sacrificing maintainability or transparency.</p><p>This is an engineering project exploring how system architecture, desktop integration, and visual design can work as parts of a unified whole.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Foundation / direction</h2><div><h3>Arch Linux</h3><p>HORUS OS is built on Arch Linux, leveraging its rolling-release model, comprehensive package ecosystem, and transparent build system. The base lets the project focus on boot workflow, desktop integration, and visual identity rather than maintaining an independent package ecosystem.</p><h3>Niri + DankMaterialShell</h3><p>The current desktop direction combines Niri, a scrollable-tiling Wayland compositor, with DankMaterialShell, a modern desktop shell. This direction is exploratory and may evolve as implementation reveals practical constraints or better alternatives.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Engineering philosophy</h2><div><h3>Deliberate decisions</h3><p>Every choice—from bootloader to desktop shell—is made with clear reasoning and documented rationale.</p><h3>Maintainable over convenient</h3><p>Long-term maintainability takes precedence over short-term convenience. Stable, documented components are preferred over hidden complexity.</p><h3>Honest communication</h3><p>Development status is communicated accurately. Planned work is not presented as completed features.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>System architecture</h2><div><h3>Boot and installation</h3><p>Boot workflow uses Limine as the bootloader. The installation process is being developed to be predictable, well-documented, and easy to validate.</p><h3>Desktop integration</h3><p>Desktop integration focuses on making Niri and DankMaterialShell work together cohesively, with consistent keyboard navigation, predictable workspace behavior, and visual continuity across system components.</p></div></section>
<section class="project-end"><p class="section-index">STATUS / IN DEVELOPMENT</p><h2>Engineering before appearances.</h2><p>Core infrastructure milestones are tracked on the <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a>. No public release is currently available.</p><a class="button button--primary" href="/roadmap/">View the roadmap ↗</a></section>
</div></main><Footer />
<script src="../scripts/ambient-background.ts"></script><script src="../scripts/precision-cursor.ts"></script>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.editorial-page { padding-bottom: var(--space-3xl); }.editorial-page .page-header { max-width: 60rem; }.editorial-page .content-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .7fr 1.3fr; gap: 4rem; }.editorial-page .content-section > div { max-width: 66ch; }.editorial-page .content-section h3 { margin-top: 2rem; }.editorial-page .content-section h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }.project-end { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .7fr 1.3fr; gap: 4rem; padding-top: var(--space-2xl); }.project-end h2 { max-width: 12ch; font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); }.project-end p:not(.section-index) { max-width: 55ch; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }.project-end .button { grid-column: 2; align-self: start; justify-self: start; width: fit-content; }.section-index { color: var(--color-gold-primary); font: .68rem var(--font-family-mono); letter-spacing: .12em; }@media(max-width:700px){.editorial-page .content-section,.project-end{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.5rem}.project-end .button{grid-column:auto}}
</style>
